
    SUBC CROSS-COMPILER TARGET ARCHITECTURE FRAMEWORK (v2)


    OVERVIEW

    This directory contains the cross-compiler target architecture
    framework for SubC. The framework uses a composable design with
    three separate components:

    1. struct cg_vtable   - Code generation function pointers
    2. struct cg_arch     - Architecture properties (CPU-specific)
    3. struct cg_os_config - Operating system configuration

    These components are combined into struct cg_target, allowing
    maximum code reuse between targets.


    KEY BENEFITS

    - Single binary supports multiple targets
    - Cross-compilation without recompiling the compiler
    - Minimal code duplication between OS variants
    - Easy addition of new architectures or OS combinations
    - Clean separation of concerns
    - Pure C89 code, no macros or preprocessor tricks


